   "textKind": "explain",
   "content": "**National governments usually spend more on heritage, but local governments lead in some countries.** National spending was higher in **30 of 37 countries** with figures for both.\n\nLocal governments supplied **88%** of the combined spending in Belgium, **75%** in Belarus and **68%** in Serbia, but only **5%** in Sweden and **3%** in Malta.\n\nLatest matched year from 2020–2024; regional governments and private money are not included. Source: UIS, February 2026 release.",
